      <activity id="b0ddeedf-7e94-5719-8bd1-092830744111" activityNameId="cd0ddabc-168a-5118-8b91-6aa91a120c1d" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Recultivation, limestone mine</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Recultivation, limestone mine
The ratio of topsoil (assumed density: 1'400 kg/m3, thickness: 0.3 m, weight: 420 kg/m2, ) to extracted limestone (density: 2'300 kg/m3, thickness: 70m, weight: 160'000 kg/m2) is about 0.26%. The diesel fuel used for covering the closed mine is thus calculated using this ratio compared to its requirement during operation of the mine.;
Synonyms: Renaturierung; 
UUID: a5b48a4d-ce72-35c9-bf9b-d397f6c5ba67
includes only transformation from mineral extraction site to forest and the diesel consumption.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Recultivation topsoil thickness 30 cm for a medium-size Swiss limestone mine .
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: survey 
Extrapolations: data which are only available for GLO have been used as proxy for CH
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_a5b48a4d-ce72-35c9-bf9b-d397f6c5ba67.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
